{"id": 17, "ts": 1780580174.279499, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s thorough recap of the strengths and concerns for each candidate. While Candidate\u202fA\u2019s technical acumen and leadership are compelling, we still have no evidence about his ability to stay calm and effective under the high\u2011pressure conditions typical of long\u2011distance flights. My recent check with Sarah confirmed that we lack any explicit information on A\u2019s stress resilience.\nIn contrast, the information James provided about Candidate\u202fD shows that he \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately,\u201d \u201cconcentrates very well,\u201d \u201csolves problems extremely well,\u201d and \u201ctakes responsibility seriously.\u201d These points collectively indicate a solid capacity to maintain performance when faced with sudden, high\u2011stress situations\u2014an essential criterion for this role. Although D\u2019s \u201chot temper\u201d and being viewed as a \u201cloner\u201d raise legitimate crew\u2011cooperation concerns, the concrete evidence of his stress handling gives us a clearer picture of his operational reliability under pressure than we have for A.\nGiven that stress resilience is a non\u2011negotiable safety requirement and we have concrete positive evidence for D but none for A, I propose we shift our provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fD**. We should still probe D\u2019s interpersonal style further, but his demonstrated ability to manage unexpected events and maintain focus makes him the stronger overall fit at this stage."}
